title: HardworkingGirl
---
<<fade_out YarnCommands 0>><<wait 1>><<picture YarnCommands placeholder>><<fade_in YarnCommands 1>><<bloom_text YarnCommands "Hardworking Girl">>
You come across a small settlement of survivors. Even in such chaotic times, people are still able to band together for survival.
As you walk past, you see groups of people working hard as their bodies sweat and tire from heavy work.
One of the workers is struggling under the weight of a large crate. He looks exhausted and could pass out at any moment.
<<jump hardworking_girl_1>>
===

title: hardworking_girl_1
---
What should you do?
-> Lend him a hand #paneldetails=Lose_10%_Vigor._Gain_2_Proficiency.
    <<change_vigor_percent -10>><<change_proficiency 2>>
    You approach him and offer some help. At first, the man is hesitant to accept help from such a young girl, but you insist.
    You take hold of the crate and help carry it across the settlement.
    By the time the crate is unloaded, the worker is already treating you like one of their own.
    Worker: "Thank you! Sorry for doubting you. Your parents must be proud!"
    You wear the smuggest grin on your face.
    <<jump hardworking_girl_2>>
-> Leave
    You are too delicate for such physical work. You pray for the man's well-being and go on your way.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
===

title: hardworking_girl_2
---
After the first delivery, another survivor approaches the man with another task.
Survivor: "Abigail needs help with inventory in the storage room, mind helpin her out?"
-> Volunteer to replace him #paneldetails=Lose_10%_Vigor._Gain_1_Abundance.
    <<change_vigor_percent -10>><<change_abundance 1>>
    You offer to take over the task. The survivor glances at you, then back at the man. He nods.
    Survivor: "Well, if you insist."
    You help organize the supplies in the storage room.
    The settlement's stores are noticeably better arranged by the time you finish.
    Scylla: "That's all of em! I could've done this myself, but thank you, little one!"
    The Scylla extends one her tentacles to shake your hand.
    <<jump hardworking_girl_3>>
-> He's had his rest. Let him work.
    The man seems motivated, let him do his part. You leave the settlement and be on your way.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
===

title: hardworking_girl_3
---
The settlement's residents begin working together more efficiently.
Nearby, a group of beastmen are carrying logs to repair a damaged structure.
-> Offer to help #paneldetails=Lose_10%_Vigor._Gain_5_Affinity.
    <<change_vigor_percent -10>><<change_affinity 5>>
    You approach the beastmen and offer to help carry the logs.
    They exchange glances with each other, unsure whether you're jesting or not.
    To break the silence, you grab one of the logs and effortlessly hoist it onto your shoulder before carrying it toward the construction site.
    The beastmen stare at you in disbelief.
    Beastman 1: "Where does all that strength come from?!"
    Beastman 2: "Unbelievable, such a frail frame, bearing all that burden..."
    Beastman 3: "You've certainly earned our respect, little one!"
    Beastman 1: "Can't let her beat us, can we?! Let's go!"
    <<jump hardworking_girl_4>>
-> They can handle it
    You've done enough here. Time to split.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
===

title: hardworking_girl_4
---
As the beatmen hype themselves up, they finish repairing the structure and head off for drinks.
The workers are now repairing the settlement's defenses.
One of the protective wards is in need of repairs. A magician stands beside a ritual circle, rummaging through her books.
-> I'm familiar with those rune patterns #paneldetails=Lose_10%_Vigor._Gain_1_Arcana_and_2_Metabolism.
    <<change_vigor_percent -10>><<change_arcana 1>><<change_metabolism 2>>
    You approach the magician and take a closer look at the ritual circle.
    You give her pointers, pointing out a few mistakes in the arrangement.
    Mage: "Wait, you're right! Ooh... I overlooked a couple of steps..."
    You help her rearrange the runes and reinforce the ritual circle.
    <<jump hardworking_girl_5>>
-> She'll figure it out
    Experience is the greatest teacher. Let her solve this predicament herself.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
===

title: hardworking_girl_5
---
As the final rune falls into place, the circle lights up, and the protective ward hums back to life.
Mage: "Incredible! Thank you, miss! I hope to become your apprentice someday!"
As you bid farewell with the mage, you hear a heated argument coming from the settlement square.
A burly man stands face-to-face with a towering demon, both refusing to back down.
Two war-weary veterans, a human and a demon, still harbor hatred for each other despite the world's descent into darkness.
-> Mediate them #paneldetails=Lose_10%_Vigor._Gain_1_Wisdom_and_1_Insight.
    <<change_vigor_percent -10>><<change_wisdom 1>><<change_insight 1>>
    You step between the two before either can make a move.
    You remind them that whatever happened during the war, the world has changed since then.
    The man slowly lowers his weapon. After a long silence, the demon lets out a frustrated growl and turns away.
    They part ways without another word, leaving the survivors to breathe a sigh of relief.
    [nomarkup]...[/nomarkup]
    You've done everything you can. This settlement has finally brimmed with the life the world you once knew.
    The survivors thank you gratefully as you wave goodbye and continue your journey.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
-> This one's out of my control...
    You decide that the settlement is at least safe enough from external dangers, let them handle the internal ones.
    <<hide_speaker_frame YarnCommands>><<wait 1>><<fade_out YarnCommands 2>><<load_map_scene>>
===
